   (From then on Spouse’s benefit adds about $22K a year in today’s dollars, so you take that much less from the accounts. The amount already assumes only 73% of the full benefit is paid by then, in case Congress does not fix the shortfall in Social Security’s trust fund. If it does, you will get more.)
> In the typical market of the table below, 2053: spent $99K; $33K from Social Security; $66K from Roth.
"
